+def viewer_clock(lines, fig_filter=None):
+    """W2 D2. The time of every "WLREMOTE fig" line of the viewer log, and of every "WLREMOTE rep" line.
+    'age' (primary, exact to the printed ms): a fig line's age = (tick now - RecvAt) + RecvAgeMs (WonderlandWorldPresence.cpp, the fig UE_LOG),
+       RecvAt is taken inside the world-report answer that delivered the figure's current position, right after that answer's own
+       "WLREMOTE send soles" line (WonderlandSocialLive.cpp), and that answer's "WLREMOTE rep" line prints RecvAgeMs as age=. So
+       t(fig) = t(that soles line, D1) + (age(fig) - age(rep)) / 1000. The delivering answer = the first rep line of the current position
+       (later rep lines of a standing player repeat it; RecvAt is not reset). Used only if the nearest anchor before the rep line in the
+       file is a "send soles" line (the same answer), the fig's printed recv equals that rep's p, the fig ages of that arrival only grow,
+       the fig line's stamp is not earlier than the time (a stamp is never early; 5 ms rounding allowance) and not before the arrival.
+    'lag' (fallback): fig stamp - the queue lag interpolated by file line between the viewer's own anchors.
+    Returns (figs {line index: (t, method, stamp)}, reps [(line index, fig, key, t or None, stamp)], counts)."""
